      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-287760",
      ":question/problem": "Two identical square-based wooden blocks are each in the shape of a right rectangular prism with a height of $20$ inches $(in)$. The surface area of each block is $Min^{2}$. When the two blocks are joined together by gluing one of their square bases together, the resulting solid has a surface area of $\\frac{12}{7}Min^{2}$. What is the side length, in inches, of each square base?"
